t_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Next, a regression test and a check across edge cases.\nFixed: `round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** `2.675` can't be stored exactly as a float. Python actually holds `2.67499999\u2026`, so `round(x, 2)` correctly rounds it down. Plain `round()` also rounds exact halves to the nearest even digit, so `round(0.125, 2)` gives `0.12`. Both go against the \"half up\" promise in the docstring.\n\n**Change** (`pricing/money.py`): `round_money` now turns the float into a `Decimal` using its shortest printed form (`repr`, which gives `\"2.675\"`). It then rounds to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP` and converts back to `float`, so the return type is the same as before. Exact negative halves now round away from zero (`-2.675` \u2192 `-2.68`). `add_vat` picks up the fix automatically, since it calls `round_money`.\n\n**Verification:** pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the test functions directly with `python3`.\n- Old behaviour reproduced: `round(2.675,2)=2.67`, `round(1.005,2)=1.0`, `round(0.125,2)=0.12`.\n- New regression test `tests/test_round_money.py` checks `2.675\u21922.68`, `1.005\u21921.01`, `0.125\u21920.13`, `2.674\u21922.67` and `-2.675\u2192-2.68`. It passes.\n- The existing `tests/test_split.py` still passes.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 253992, "requests_cache_write": 8269, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1398634, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 2382, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial10", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 19, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T06:09:09.080422+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 